message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
title: "Which String Vibrations Become Which Generations on the Dwork Quintic: code, checks and engine record"
abstract: >-
  Code, independent checks and the record of the Anaxia engine for the paper
  "Which String Vibrations Become Which Generations on the Dwork Quintic".
  The paper proves that the 101 generations of the heterotic string on the
  quintic pencil carry 101 distinct characters of the symmetry group
  (Z/5)^3, that every Yukawa coupling allowed by the symmetry is a power of
  the modulus and every other coupling vanishes (1431 nonzero couplings),
  that the invariant direction pairs each generation with exactly one
  partner, so that the mass matrix has determinant psi^70 and rank 51 at the
  Fermat point, where the masses are given by the Gamma function, and that
  the Geometric Selection Conjecture is equivalent to the existence of one
  viable vacuum fixed by mirror symmetry. On the sextic, octic and dectic
  pencils of Fermat type in weighted projective space the symmetry no
  longer separates the generations (96, 122 and 100 characters for 103, 149
  and 145 generations), the mass map of the invariant direction has rank
  99, 125 and 109, and no member or free quotient carries three families.
  The archive holds 121 independent checks in C, C++, Python, Julia,
  Macaulay2 and shell, 14 Lean 4 theorems, and the failure, change and
  retry record of the five targets on the Anaxia engine.
